
Whenever you want to debug your application ?
- 1st rule run application in debug mode.


                                      BASIC DEBUGGER
🔴 BreakPoint :
         - Jis line par tum chahte ho ki code execution temporarily ruk jaye jab tum request bhejo (API call karo), wahan breakpoint lagate ho.

🔕 Mute Breakpoint :
          - Ye temporarily saare breakpoints disable kar deta hai bina unhe delete kiye.

Threads & Variables shows :
             - It shows the currently active execution threads and the runtime values of variables at the breakpoint.


Debugger Actions / Debugging Controls
   ▶ Resume Program :
              - Resume Program is a debugger action.
              - it is jump to one break-point to another break-point.
              - Breakpoint lagaya,Debug mode me run kiya,Code ruk gaya,▶ (Resume) dabaya,Code next breakpoint tak run karega.
   ⏸ Pause Program :
              - Pause Program is a debugger action.
              - used to temporarily suspend a running application to inspect.

   1️⃣ Step Over (F8) :
                 - Step Over is a debugger action.
                 - used to execute the current line of code(line by line) without entering into any called method.
   2️⃣ Step Into (F7) :
                 - Step Into is a debugger action.
                 - used to enter inside the called method to debug its internal implementation.
   3️⃣ Step Out (Shift + F8) :
                 - Step Out is a debugger action.
                 - used to exit the current method and return to the calling method.

🎯 What is Evaluate Expression?
Evaluate Expression debugger ka feature hai jo tumhe :
                  - runtime ke time,current execution context me,koi bhi expression run karke result dekhne deta hai.
                  - Ex->
                      Method manually call karna  : orderService.getAllOrders()
                      Complex logic test karna :   user.getOrders().stream().filter(o -> o.getPrice() > 5000).toList()


